Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||05-24-2001||09:31 PM||||Hi, I'd like to dress up the engine bay (and protect my wiring at the same time) using stainless hose but realized that I have no idea how much and what sizes to order.  If anyone has a list of the lengths and widths of the main wiring components in the engine, or pictures of a stock fiero engine that has been dressed up this way please post it to me.  I found this stuff in Summit Racing magazine.<BR>Thanks a million,<BR>Mike Schaefer||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||05-24-2001||10:50 PM||||They sell it in Pep boys with random lengths and widths for the coolant hoses, including all of the end clamps.  The easiest way to do it is by taking off the coolant hoses, rather than try it on the engine.  you can also buy different color silicon vacuum lines.  Have you thought of getting real braided hose rather than the cover up stuff?  I know it's more money but it also looks better and serves a purpose. Just my 2 cents.  Actually less than that, I'm Canadian.  Let's see, exchange rate about 55%  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">, time to buy Canadian products.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||05-24-2001||11:53 PM||||Doing a little engine clean-up myself!<BR>Here's a few pics:<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=49125558&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=49125629&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=49125572&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||MikeSchaefer||05-25-2001||01:24 PM||||That's a great looking engine DXR!  I never really knew about the real stainless hose, does that go over the existing lines or replace them?  How much of a price difference is there?  I really just wanted to get some major heat protection for the wiring, I have had bad luck with my past three Fieros because of a few bad wires.<BR>Thanks for the help,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
